      "textInput": " 𝐌𝐀𝐉𝐎𝐑 𝐁𝐑𝐄𝐀𝐊𝐈𝐍𝐆 | 𝐋𝐀 𝐋𝐈𝐆𝐀 𝐂𝐈𝐕𝐈𝐋 𝐖𝐀𝐑: Javier Tebas leaks official invoices in late-night attack on Real Madrid! 🤬⚖️💥\r\n\r\nThe war between La Liga’s President and Real Madrid has gone from verbal barbs to leaked corporate paper trails. Tebas hit back at a prominent Madrid account, calling its followers \"bootlickers\" before uploading the club's official invoices:\r\n\r\n📉 𝐓𝐡𝐞 𝐅𝐢𝐧𝐚𝐧𝐜𝐢𝐚𝐥 𝐏𝐫𝐨𝐨𝐟 𝐄𝐱𝐩𝐨𝐬𝐞𝐝:\r\n\r\n1️⃣ 𝐈𝐧𝐯𝐨𝐢𝐜𝐞 𝟏𝟖𝟎𝟏𝐆𝟐𝟓𝟖 (𝐉𝐚𝐧 𝟐𝟎𝟏𝟖): Shows Real Madrid billing Audiovisual New Aged €5,243.31 for a formal financial guarantee presented to the State Tax Agency (AEAT).\r\n\r\n2️⃣ 𝐈𝐧𝐯𝐨𝐢𝐜𝐞 𝐀𝐈𝐄 𝟑𝟒 (𝐃𝐞𝐜 𝟐𝟎𝟏𝟖): Shows the company billing Real Madrid €68,293.63 (including 21% VAT) for seasonal operating expenses, addressed directly to Managing Director José Ángel Sánchez (JAS).\r\n\r\n🫵 \"𝐄𝐯𝐞𝐫𝐲𝐨𝐧𝐞 𝐏𝐚𝐢𝐝 𝐄𝐱𝐜𝐞𝐩𝐭 𝐑𝐞𝐚𝐥 𝐌𝐚𝐝𝐫𝐢𝐝\": Tebas insists these documents prove the financial relationship worked both ways, claiming the fund triggered a massive tax inspection where every club took out loans to cover settlements except Real Madrid.\r\n\r\n📧 𝐓𝐡𝐞 𝐄𝐱𝐞𝐜𝐮𝐭𝐢𝐯𝐞 𝐓𝐡𝐫𝐞𝐚𝐭: Tebas has publicly challenged RM directors JAS and Chitín del Valle to explain the full email threads behind these transactions, warning: \"When you tell this story, tell it whole... I'm sure it will continue.\" 🍿🍿"
    },
    "result": {
      "format": "executive",
      "length": "detailed",
      "outputFilename": "summary.txt",
      "summary": "EXECUTIVE SUMMARY BRIEF\n==================================================\n\n🎯 CORE FOCUS:\n𝐌𝐀𝐉𝐎𝐑 𝐁𝐑𝐄𝐀𝐊𝐈𝐍𝐆 | 𝐋𝐀 𝐋𝐈𝐆𝐀 𝐂𝐈𝐕𝐈𝐋 𝐖𝐀𝐑: Javier Tebas leaks official invoices in late-night attack on Real Madrid.\n\n📊 KEY HIGHLIGHTS:\n• 1️⃣ 𝐈𝐧𝐯𝐨𝐢𝐜𝐞 𝟏𝟖𝟎𝟏𝐆𝟐𝟓𝟖 (𝐉𝐚𝐧 𝟐𝟎𝟏𝟖): Shows Real Madrid billing Audiovisual New Aged €5,243.31 for a formal financial guarantee presented to the State Tax Agency (AEAT).\n• 2️⃣ 𝐈𝐧𝐯𝐨𝐢𝐜𝐞 𝐀𝐈𝐄 𝟑𝟒 (𝐃𝐞𝐜 𝟐𝟎𝟏𝟖): Shows the company billing Real Madrid €68,293.63 (including 21% VAT) for seasonal operating expenses, addressed directly to Managing Director José Ángel Sánchez (JAS).\n• 🫵 \"𝐄𝐯𝐞𝐫𝐲𝐨𝐧𝐞 𝐏𝐚𝐢𝐝 𝐄𝐱𝐜𝐞𝐩𝐭 𝐑𝐞𝐚𝐥 𝐌𝐚𝐝𝐫𝐢𝐝\": Tebas insists these documents prove the financial relationship worked both ways, claiming the fund triggered a massive tax inspection where every club took out loans to cover settlements except Real Madrid.\n• 📧 𝐓𝐡𝐞 𝐄𝐱𝐞𝐜𝐮𝐭𝐢𝐯𝐞 𝐓𝐡𝐫𝐞𝐚𝐭: Tebas has publicly challenged RM directors JAS and Chitín del Valle to explain the full email threads behind these transactions, warning: \"When you tell this story, tell it whole.\n",
      "wordCount": 156
    }
